  "body": "Refs #787 — Slice D only (cross-language parity oracle). This PR does **not** close #787: Slices E/F remain, gated on F13.4 detection (#786).\n\n## What\n\nPer design `doc/2026-11-01_design_id787.md` §6 row D:\n\n- **Corpus** (`doc/kitty-disambiguate-v1-fixtures.json`): 24 of the 40 cases gain a `browser` field — the browser key event for the same keystroke plus the exact bytes the Slice C rich encoder must emit (the encoder's canonical form where the fixture's terminal input is an alternate form, e.g. F1 tilde vs letter).\n- **Roc oracle** (`pkgs/id/scripts/key-parity-generate.py` + `key-parity-test.sh`): generates one `expect` per case into a scratch copy of `examples/roc-world/Key.roc` and runs the pinned `roc test` — terminal bytes and browser bytes both decode through the **actual compiled `Key.parse_events`**, never a re-implemented decoder. Comparison zeroes the per-event `source` (which byte form produced the event); parity = key + modifiers + kind, plus `EventUnknown` payloads. Missing roc/python3/corpus/Key.roc **fails loudly**; a shrunk corpus (<40 terminal / <20 browser cases) is **refused** — no silent skips, no weakened oracle. Wired into `scripts/roc-test.sh`.\n- **Web twin** (`pkgs/id/web/src/world-keyboard.parity.test.ts`): pins `richTerminalBytesForKey` to the corpus bytes for every browser case and guards corpus completeness (same pattern as the screen-parity twin).\n\n## Verification (laptop, `nix develop`, worktree off origin/main)\n\n- Generated Roc run: **123/123 passed** (59 original Key expects + 64 generated parity expects: 40 terminal + 24 browser).\n- Negative controls: mutated corpus expectation → Roc run fails (2 failed); 10-case corpus → generator refuses (exit 1).\n- Full `scripts/roc-test.sh`: RocJson 29, Screen 15, Key 59, **key-parity 123**, roc-cap-demo — all passed in sequence (the final pre-existing roc-import-policy cargo section was still compiling under load at merge time; this diff touches none of its inputs).\n- vitest: parity **25/25**, existing world-keyboard **22/22**; `tsc --noEmit` clean; biome clean; shellcheck + shfmt clean.\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://dashboardbackend.blacksmith.sh/track/run-proof?expires=1798002738&installation_model_id=443529&pr_number=12926&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=developing-today%2Fcode&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fdeveloping-today%2Fcode%2Fpull%2F12926&variant=get_evidence&signature=ff3a2b700bb65a16536dd19b0cbb072f7e1533b52230c1a6cd168b9815b8ce37\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/proof-get-evidence-v2-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/proof-get-evidence-v2-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Get evidence\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/proof-get-evidence-v2-dark-3x.png\" width=\"123\" height=\"28\"></picture></a>\n<sup><a href=\"https://app.blacksmith.sh/developing-today/codesmith/code/pr/12926?autoLogin=true&ref=codesmith_pr_footer\">Open in [code]smith</a> · Need help on this PR? Tag <code>@codesmith-bot</code> with what you need.</sup>\n\n<!-- codesmith:autofix:disabled -->\n<!-- /codesmith:footer -->",
